# Deployment is not part of this repository. Note this is NOT because hosting is
# out of scope — that call was reversed on 2026-08-11 and the app is deployed.
# It is because the deployment is specific to one private AWS account that also
# runs an unrelated product: variables.tf, deploy.sh and the runbook carry that
# account id, the instance id, the domain and the other product's topology.
#
# The state files are the second reason, and the reason this is a whole-directory
# rule rather than a list: `terraform.tfstate` records generated database
# passwords and account identifiers in plaintext, and a rule that names files can
# only protect the files somebody remembered to name.
#
# The dev stack is unaffected: docker-compose.yml lives at the repo root and is
# tracked, which is what `make setup` runs. Everything under infra/ keeps working
# locally — it is untracked, not deleted. Runbook: docs/DEPLOY.md (also ignored).
infra/
.dockerignore
